WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.920
458 scans map which hypothelamic regions shrink first in aging and Alzheimer's. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 249. A pan cancer cell atlas, gut microbes handling plant steriles, potatoes grown in lunar dust, and a spotlight on wild bees. Hypothelamic sub-regions that govern metabolism, stress and circadian rhythms, showed the largest volume loss and transcriptional shifts in a nature atlas built from high-resolution magnetic resonance imaging.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.720
or MRI, and single nucleus RNA sequencing.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:41.720
The sequencing ran on 614,403 nuclei, and mapped those nuclei onto subregions instead of

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.440
treating the hypothalamus as a single block of tissue.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.940
Microglia in the same maps adopted a pro-inflammatory state.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.660
Inhibitory neurons in sleep and circadian regulating areas displayed the strongest gene expression

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.400
changes of the cell type scored.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:03.480
The Atlas links those cellular patterns to the sleep, metabolic, and neuroendocrine disturbances seen in patients.

00:01:04.578 --> 00:01:12.578
A pan cancer Atlas of the tumor microenvironment identified conserved stromal and immune transcriptional programs in human and mouse tumors.

00:01:13.178 --> 00:01:19.818
The build integrated 3,381 single cell samples and covered more than 15 million cells.

00:01:19.818 --> 00:01:22.858
Those samples span 42 cancer types.

00:01:23.198 --> 00:01:28.078
The resource is released as an interactive web atlas that highlights subpopulations linked

00:01:28.078 --> 00:01:29.118
to poorer outcomes.

00:01:29.638 --> 00:01:34.278
Software goes with the atlas so other groups can keep interrogating the same microenvironment

00:01:34.278 --> 00:01:34.818
programs.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:42.102
Intestinal microbes in work described by Fizz.org transform phytosterols from vegetable oils,

00:01:42.482 --> 00:01:46.182
nuts and seeds into sulfated metabolites that reach distant tissues.

00:01:46.182 --> 00:01:52.342
use. Yesterday's waste water maps from eight Ohio cities serving 1.3 million people tied

00:01:52.342 --> 00:01:57.762
gut bacteria patterns to local disease rates. This tracing study adds a chemical route those

00:01:57.762 --> 00:02:03.242
microbes take with plant sterols. The route had not been mapped as a path of sterile metabolism,

00:02:03.842 --> 00:02:09.510
and it may influence systemic cholesterol handling. Something most people get wrong is the idea

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:14.250
that plant sterols only block cholesterol uptake in the intestine and then leave the

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:19.770
body unused. The steriles are first partially metabolized, and only after that step do

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:25.710
specific bacterial enzymes act. Those enzymes add sulfate groups, and the sulfated forms

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:31.210
are ones the host can absorb. About 5% of ingested phytosterols normally reach the blood

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.810
stream. The microbial root accounts for a measurable share of that circulating pool.

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:41.470
The conversion adds a previously underappreciated layer to how dietary plant steriles influence

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:47.370
systemic lipid metabolism. Maintaining dietary fiber diversity supports the bacterial species

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:52.530
capable of these conversions, and may affect how much of the sterile metabolites appear in blood.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:58.674
Potato plants reached full growth and yield in lunar regolith simulants when vermicompost was

00:02:58.674 --> 00:03:04.054
mixed into the mix. The trials used five simulants representing mare and highland regions,

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:10.454
and the full cycle appeared when 30% vermicompost was added. Plants grown with no amendment showed

00:03:10.454 --> 00:03:12.354
stunting and underdeveloped roots.

00:03:12.974 --> 00:03:17.194
Mixes of 5-15% vermicompose produced only partial recovery.

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:22.714
The organic matter binds heavy metals in the regolith, limiting toxicity while preserving

00:03:22.714 --> 00:03:28.154
nutritional quality of the tubers, and no statistically significant rise in glycoalkaloid

00:03:28.154 --> 00:03:29.334
toxins was detected.

00:03:29.854 --> 00:03:35.114
The comparison standard was high yield earth soil from Hermiston, Oregon, and the compost

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:40.094
itself is framed as recycled crew waste for institute food production on lunar missions.

00:03:40.947 --> 00:03:45.887
University of Missouri researchers found that greater access to arts classes correlated with

00:03:45.887 --> 00:03:51.147
fewer disciplinary incidents among students with disabilities. The same access lined up with

00:03:51.147 --> 00:03:57.202
higher school attendance. Writing performance improved in that group as well. Rising temperatures,

00:03:57.502 --> 00:04:02.542
extreme heat events, and habitat loss could increase the likelihood that deadly viruses carried by

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:08.182
bats reach human populations. That result comes from Adelaide University modeling of climate

00:04:08.182 --> 00:04:13.936
and habitat pressure on spillover risk. An international team examined how reintroducing

00:04:13.936 --> 00:04:19.336
large herbivores might help maintain open landscapes and lower wildfire risk in rural Europe.

00:04:20.016 --> 00:04:24.256
The work draws on ecosystem service models published in ecosystem services.

00:04:25.184 --> 00:04:29.964
Canadian antibiotic sales in food animals fell 11% since 2018.

00:04:29.964 --> 00:04:30.124
15.

00:04:30.764 --> 00:04:33.864
Federal policy changes were not the main driver of that drop.

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:38.364
Sales declined steadily through voluntary industry and veterinary actions.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:44.170
Fault motion dating in the Central Tarrities identified an earlier phase of lateral crustal

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:45.150
movement in Turkey.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:49.390
That phase ran between the early ESC and the early Maya scene.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:55.730
The dates pushed the onset of regional extension back to roughly 25 million years ago and revised

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.910
the mountain building timeline those calcite deposits record.

00:05:00.545 --> 00:05:05.945
micropeleontologists working in Portuguese sea cliffs uncovered 115 million year old algae

00:05:05.945 --> 00:05:12.465
fossils. The find is described as an unexpected algae rebellion. It pushes back the known appearance

00:05:12.465 --> 00:05:18.913
of certain algal lineages. Wild bees in rare alkaline grasslands keep more species when those

00:05:18.913 --> 00:05:24.073
habitat stay connected and are managed extensively rather than abandoned or farmed hard.

00:05:24.713 --> 00:05:29.313
A University of Gotting in Lead study in the Journal of Applied Ecology found that long

00:05:29.313 --> 00:05:35.813
term abandonment reduces B diversity in calcareous grasslands. Intensive farming cuts diversity

00:05:35.813 --> 00:05:42.213
in the same habitats. Moderate grazing supports richer pollinator communities. Nearby wildflower

00:05:42.213 --> 00:05:46.653
corridors add to that richness when they sit close enough for bees to move between patches.

00:05:47.687 --> 00:05:52.547
In a short run of other briefs, the Manchester Institute of Biotechnology marks 20 years

00:05:52.547 --> 00:05:58.167
of interdisciplinary work. With the University of Manchester Center now supporting roughly 400

00:05:58.167 --> 00:06:04.267
researchers, more than 120 million pounds in active grants, and 16 spinout companies

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:10.047
focused on sustainable chemistry, global health manufacturing, and non-invasive disease detection.

00:06:10.787 --> 00:06:15.847
Johns Hopkins researchers expanded a Korea collaboration on organ chip and mitochondrial

00:06:15.847 --> 00:06:20.847
editing tools, as nine faculty members presented joint projects on neuroimaging,

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:26.447
organoids, and convergence diagnostics during a summit that also produced a new memorandum

00:06:26.447 --> 00:06:28.487
with the Daydok R&amp;D Zone.

